###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training on one NVIDIA Tesla V100-SXM2-32GB per model; durations are in
# the trainingHardware of each run (QM9 1 h to 3 days, MD17 4 h to about
# 2.6 days, ISO17 about 7 days, ethanol about 4.5 h). Energy and gradient for
# structures of up to 100,000 atoms take less than 230 s on one Intel Xeon
# E5-2670 CPU (Sec. 2.4); the model timed is not identified, so the timing
# is held in the encoding input.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - GM-NN is introduced as a new descriptor with atom-centred feed-forward networks; no derivation from a registry method (such as HDNNP) is stated.
# - QM9 models are trained on energies only (wF = 0). Only the GM-sNN shallow network is used for QM9 and MD17 with 1,000 samples.
# - Standard deviations over the training-set draws (Tables 2, 3) are not encoded. The ethanol models' results are rotational barriers (Table 4) and a vibrational spectrum, not error metrics.
# - The QM9 and ISO17 levels of theory are not stated in this paper. The descriptor uses 427 Gaussian moments (input neurons); hidden layers are [256, 128] for GM-sNN and [1024, 512, 256, 128, 64] for GM-dNN.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zaverkin2020.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

